# Lab 03 — Least-Privilege Access

## Objective

Demonstrate how Azure RBAC access should be designed around the **minimum required permissions and minimum practical scope**.

The lab will compare a broad authorization model with a narrower model and document the security reasoning behind the final design.

---

## Learning Objectives

By the end of this lab, I will be able to:

- Explain least privilege in Azure RBAC.
- Identify excessive permissions.
- Select a narrower role where appropriate.
- Reduce scope where practical.
- Validate that required access remains available.
- Identify the security impact of excessive privileges.
- Document an authorization decision.

---

## 1. Least-Privilege Model

Use this decision process:

```text
Required business/technical task
            ↓
Required Azure actions
            ↓
Candidate role
            ↓
Smallest practical scope
            ↓
Role assignment
            ↓
Access validation
            ↓
Periodic review
            ↓
Removal when no longer required
```

The objective is not simply to reduce the role name.

The objective is to reduce the **actual permissions and blast radius** while retaining required functionality.

---

